{
  "about": "Shared vectors for specHash (packages/protocol/src/spec-hash.ts) and the Mac's twin: each `input`, its JCS text (RFC 8785, keys by UTF-16 code units) and its hash, \"sha256:\" + hex of the JCS text's UTF-8 bytes. `undefined_paths`: places (key and index paths) the test sets to an absent (undefined) value before hashing: a key is left out, an array item reads as null. `must_throw`: inputs specHash must refuse (`replace` puts a value JSON cannot hold at `path` first). Written by an independent Python reading of RFC 8785 (Hestia, 2026-11-14) and checked against the TS jcs.",
  "vectors": [
    {
      "name": "minimal",
      "note": "empty argv, env and files",
      "input": {
        "v": 1,
        "argv": [],
        "env": {},
        "files": {}
      },
      "jcs": "{\"argv\":[],\"env\":{},\"files\":{},\"v\":1}",
      "hash": "sha256:bb5d7bbd1a59df1946d506a9e8c0fe3fb6ea23090f7ccc78c679f22ba5c379ee"
    },
